WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.048
Relationships map object references to foreign keys or join tables.

00:00:04.198 --> 00:00:07.552
The owning side determines which mapping writes the relationship.

00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:12.391
For a typical one-to-many and many-to-one pair, the many-to-one side owns the

00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:15.518
foreign key, while mappedBy identifies the inverse collection.

00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:18.824
Keep both object sides consistent through helper methods.

00:00:18.974 --> 00:00:24.188
Cascade controls which entity operations propagate; it is not database foreign-key cascading

00:00:24.188 --> 00:00:28.099
and does not mean every relationship should use CascadeType.ALL.

00:00:28.249 --> 00:00:32.710
Orphan removal deletes children removed from an owned collection and should match

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:33.454
aggregate semantics.

00:00:33.604 --> 00:00:36.910
Avoid cascading removal from an order to a shared product.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:41.429
The supplied checkout starts with one product per order to keep distributed

00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:42.157
behavior visible.

00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:47.228
The relationship extension adds OrderLine children owned by PurchaseOrder, with each line

00:00:47.228 --> 00:00:50.098
storing a product identifier and price snapshot.

00:00:50.248 --> 00:00:54.705
Product remains owned by inventory and is not a JPA relationship across

00:00:54.705 --> 00:00:55.076
services.

00:00:55.226 --> 00:00:58.254
Implement OrderLine with quantity and price snapshot.

00:00:58.404 --> 00:01:01.315
Add a helper that sets both order.lines and line.order.

00:01:01.465 --> 00:01:05.810
Test adding a line, removing a line, and deleting an order without

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:07.259
deleting any catalog product.

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:10.200
Use aggregate ownership for cascade decisions.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.809
A line belongs to one order and may be deleted with it;

00:01:13.809 --> 00:01:15.827
a product is shared and independently managed.

00:01:15.977 --> 00:01:18.621
Add migrations and test foreign-key behavior.

00:01:18.771 --> 00:01:22.083
Do not expose the bidirectional graph directly as JSON.

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:22.905
Question.

00:01:23.055 --> 00:01:24.439
What does mappedBy mean?

00:01:24.589 --> 00:01:25.165
Answer.

00:01:25.315 --> 00:01:29.112
It names the property on the owning side of a bidirectional relationship;

00:01:29.112 --> 00:01:31.327
it is not the database column name.

00:01:31.477 --> 00:01:32.148
Question.

00:01:32.298 --> 00:01:34.924
Why store a price snapshot on an order line?

00:01:35.074 --> 00:01:35.651
Answer.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:39.738
The order must preserve the agreed purchase price even when the catalog

00:01:39.738 --> 00:01:40.722
price later changes.
